What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/63400000.efuse/soc_uid
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        UDX710 board maintainers
Description:
                Read-only SoC UID for the Orca eFuse variant. The file mode is
                0400 and its size is exactly 8 bytes. It contains two
                little-endian 32-bit words: physical eFuse block 0 followed by
                block 1, with bit 31 cleared in each word. The controller reads
                both blocks in double mode, matching the board's original
                U-Boot READ_UID response. Partial reads are supported.

                Hardware lock, clock and controller failures return an error
                without exposing partial UID bytes. All-zero or all-one masked
                UID values return ENODATA. This interface never programs eFuse.

                The existing orca-public-efuse calibration provider retains
                its 180-byte aperture at physical blocks 2 through 46. Its
                offset 0 is not the UID. CONFIG_NVMEM_SYSFS is not required for
                this dedicated attribute.
